# --- files the image build needs, kept in the context on purpose ------------
#
# `.dockerignore` has no per-stage syntax, so anything ignored here is missing
# from BOTH stages. The build stage runs the full suite
# (`RUN pnpm typecheck && pnpm test`), which means every file the tests read has
# to survive this list:
#
#   fixtures/            -> read by the streaming/chat/messages suites
#   tests/               -> the suite itself
#   Dockerfile,          -> scanned by tests/leak-scan.test.ts, whose whole job
#   docker-compose.yml      is to prove no credential is baked into them
#
# Excluding any of these made the build fail: first `"/fixtures": not found` at
# the COPY, then ENOENT from the leak scan. They are safe to leave in because the
# runtime stage never copies them — it takes only `src`, the public config, and
# the entrypoint — so nothing here reaches the shipped image.
